---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	lang="en"
	title="About — František Bolgac"
	description="František Bolgac on technology, AI and data sovereignty."
>
	<article class="about-page">
		<p class="eyebrow">About</p>
		<h1>I am František Bolgac.</h1>
		<p class="lead">
			I worked as an enterprise IT administrator. Today I run my own business and focus on the
			practical use of AI in companies. I am interested in how to benefit from technology
			without companies losing control of their data.
		</p>

		<div class="content">
			<h2>I start with data</h2>
			<p>
				When designing a solution, I first ask: <strong>What data do we have? Who may access it?
				Where can it go? What do we need to do with it?</strong> Only then do I choose the
				architecture, AI tools and the place where the data will be processed.
			</p>
			<p>
				I use this approach in my own business as well as in work on software for legal environments,
				pseudonymisation of sensitive data and AI agents. I am interested in solutions that work in
				everyday operations, not only in a demonstration.
			</p>

			<h2>What I write about</h2>
			<p>
				On this blog I discuss my decisions, experiences and the limits of tools. I also write
				about when the cloud makes sense, when local processing makes sense and what a company
				needs to know before entrusting its data to AI.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>AI where it makes sense. Cloud where it makes sense. Local processing where data
				must not leave the company.</strong>
			</p>
		</div>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.about-page {
		padding: 1rem 0;
	}
	.eyebrow {
		margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
		color: var(--accent);
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}
	h1 {
		max-width: 24ch;
		margin: 0;
		font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
		letter-spacing: -0.04em;
	}
	.lead {
		max-width: 42rem;
		margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: 1.125rem;
	}
	.content {
		max-width: 42rem;
		margin-top: 3rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
		padding-top: 2rem;
	}
	.content h2 {
		margin: 2rem 0 0;
		font-size: 1.5rem;
	}
	.content h2:first-child {
		margin-top: 0;
	}
	.content p {
		margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
		color: var(--muted);
	}
</style>
